@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+## Why
+
+A task is only referred to by its title, so a reference breaks when the task is renamed. The app needs a stable reference.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets a unique string `id`, set by `add` and never changed (rename keeps it).
+- The list gets `get(id)`, returning a `Result<Task>` like its other methods.
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-identity`: unique, stable task ids and looking up tasks by them.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/domain/task.ts` (`Task` gains `id`), `src/domain/list.ts`, tests. Existing tests that compare whole tasks need the `id`.
